jobs.description:
What will you do?

As an Operator, you will work in a dynamic production environment within the fresh produce industry (potatoes, vegetables, and fruit). You will play an important role in the sorting process of avocados and mangoes, ensuring that production runs smoothly and efficiently.

During your first week, you will work on the sorting line to gain a thorough understanding of the production process. You will sort fruit based on its ripeness while learning how the sorting department operates. After this onboarding period, you will be paired with an experienced buddy who will guide and support you until you are confident enough to work independently.

Your responsibilities include:

- Working on the sorting line during your onboarding period, sorting fruit based on ripeness;
- Receiving and processing production orders using the computer;
- Translating production orders into clear instructions for the sorting team;
- Supervising a sorting line of approximately 7 employees;
- Monitoring the quality and progress of the production process.

This is a varied role in which you will combine hands-on production work with team leadership. You will continuously switch between planning, execution, and coordinating your team to ensure production targets are met.

Working Days & Hours

You will work 38 hours per week, Monday through Friday, with occasional Saturdays when required.

Working hours: 06:45 AM – 03:30 PM, with occasional overtime until production has been completed.

- Available to work 38 hours per week, Monday through Friday (occasional Saturdays);
- Comfortable working with computers;
- Good command of Dutch and/or English;
- Experience in the fresh produce industry is an advantage;
- Experience as an Operator or in a supervisory role;
- Able to lead and motivate a team;
- Stress-resistant and able to adapt to changing circumstances.

Are you an enthusiastic Order Picker with EPT experience, or are you eager to learn? We are looking for motivated candidates to join a modern logistics company in Helmond. As an Order Picker with EPT, you will be responsible for collecting, checking, and moving goods throughout the warehouse. Your work ensures that customer orders are processed accurately and shipped on time.

Your responsibilities:

- Picking customer orders using a handheld scanner;
- Checking orders before shipment;
- Moving goods and pallets using an Electric Pallet Truck (EPT);
- Wrapping, labeling, and scanning pallets;
- Performing Value Added Services (VAS) activities;
- Supporting various warehouse and logistics processes;
- Maintaining a clean, safe, and organized working environment.

Working Hours in the regular day shift: 07:00 AM – 04:00 PM. During peak periods in July till October, a two-shift schedule applies:

- 06:00 AM – 03:00 PM
- 03:00 PM – 12:00 AM

- Has experience operating an EPT or is willing to learn;
- Fulltime available;
- Is flexible regarding tasks and working hours;
- Performs well under pressure;
- Enjoys working in a team;
- Has a good command of Dutch and/or English;
- Has a proactive and hands-on attitude.

As a Forklift and/or Reach Truck Operator, you are responsible for keeping the warehouse and shipping process running efficiently. Your daily tasks include collecting and moving goods, scanning shipments, checking orders for accuracy, loading and unloading trucks, and maintaining a clean and safe working environment. You are also happy to support other departments whenever needed, because teamwork is at the heart of DSV.

You will work full-time (40 hours per week) in a fixed team at the Moerdijk warehouse and are willing to work in a two-shift schedule.

- Valid Forklift and/or Reach Truck certificate;
- At least 1 year of experience operating a forklift or reach truck;
- Full-time availability (40 hours per week) willing to work a fixed two-shift schedule (06:00 - 15:00, 07:00 - 16:00, 08:00 - 17:00, or 15:00 - 00:00);
- Own transportation and willingness to work in Moerdijk;
- You are at least 18 years old and a VMBO or MBO working thinking level (or equivalent);
- You have a good command of the English language;
- Accurate, safety-conscious, and a team player;
